  modes:
  - key: light
    tokens:
      colours:
      - name: --ts-bg
        value: {r: 0.95686275, g: 0.9411765, b: 0.9098039, a: 1}
        note: 'Surfaces (_3.3 P4.4b, measured: ThemeContrastTests)'
      - name: --ts-surface
        value: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
        note: 'A block: the opaque surface inside its rim (R12.5)'
      - name: --ts-surface-2
        value: {r: 0.95686275, g: 0.9411765, b: 0.9098039, a: 1}
        note: Buttons, chips and wells on a block
      - name: --ts-scrim
        value: {r: 0, g: 0, b: 0, a: 0.7}
        note: 'The scrim under a menu over the card (_3.2 step 8). The project renders
          in LINEAR colour, so an alpha blends in linear light: 0.5 left the card''s
          text behind at 181 of 247 (measured), still competing with the menu; 0.7
          recedes it to a frame (about 144)'
      - name: --ts-scrim-hero
        value: {r: 0.039215688, g: 0.031372547, b: 0.023529412, a: 0.94}
        note: 'The dark of the hero: the colour of Words On Picture''s tone and scrim
          (their strength is the picture''s own, worked out per hero), the ground
          of a Clear Navigation Bar at Top over the hero, and the ink of the bar''s
          disc there. The alpha is that ground''s: the project blends in LINEAR light,
          so it is chosen against the WORST pixel any picture can have, pure white
          -- at 0.94 the ground stays at luminance 0.062 and the white words keep
          7:1 over any picture (ThemeContrastTests). The same in both modes: the
          hero is a picture'
      - name: --ts-on-scrim
        value: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
        note: The hero's title, line and outline button over the scrim
      - name: --ts-on-scrim-2
        value: {r: 0.94509804, g: 0.9137255, b: 0.85490197, a: 1}
        note: The hero's eyebrow over the scrim (a warm white)
      - name: --ts-hero-glow
        value: {r: 0.039215688, g: 0.03137255, b: 0.023529412, a: 0.72}
        note: 'The ground of the hero''s focal action (its thin outline button):
          a dark see-through fill over the picture'
      - name: --ts-text-halo
        value: {r: 0, g: 0, b: 0, a: 0.85}
        note: 'The dark halo hugging every letter of the hero (its text-shadow):
          the picture right around a word is darkened, so the word reads over a bright
          sky'
      - name: --ts-bar
        value: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
        note: 'The card''s chrome ground: the grabber row, the bar, the top strip,
          the footer -- opaque, so their words never sit on the glass'
      - name: --ts-button-glass
        value: {r: 0.078431375, g: 0.06666667, b: 0.050980393, a: 0.07}
        note: 'The round buttons'' ground on a see-through bar (X, settings, menu):
          a faint disc, no rim -- the solid mark carries the button'
      - name: --ts-top-shade
        value: {r: 0, g: 0, b: 0, a: 0.5}
        note: 'The fade from the sheet top while the floating bars sit on the hero
          picture (tints top_shade.png): their white marks read on any picture'
      - name: --ts-chrome-glass
        value: {r: 0.98039216, g: 0.972549, b: 0.95686275, a: 0.72}
        note: 'The chrome discs after the hero (_3.3 S4 third round, v5): the X and
          settings on light glass (smoked in dark), the mark in the card''s ink'
      - name: --ts-chrome-band
        value: {r: 0.98039216, g: 0.972549, b: 0.95686275, a: 0.94}
        note: 'The band behind the chrome row after the hero (_3.3 S4 third round,
          v5: light glass, the title centred, a hairline at its foot): DENSE, so
          no block text reads through it (no backdrop blur in UI Toolkit) and the
          marks and the title keep 7:1 over anything scrolling under it (PoiCardChromeMarksSceneTests)'
      - name: --ts-top-fade
        value: {r: 0.95686275, g: 0.9411765, b: 0.9098039, a: 1}
        note: 'The fade band behind the chrome row after the hero (_3.3 S4 third
          round, v6 Top Band = Fade): the sheet''s own colour, opaque (the ramp card_top_fade.png
          carries the alpha: solid through the row, then fading to nothing, no edge)'
      - name: --ts-navbar-glass
        value: {r: 0.98039216, g: 0.972549, b: 0.95686275, a: 0.72}
        note: 'A Glass Navigation Bar once the hero is read (_3.3 S4 third round):
          v5''s light glass in light mode; in dark, smoked glass dense enough that
          its light words keep 7:1 over a bright picture scrolling under it -- no
          backdrop blur in UI Toolkit (PoiCardNavBarSceneTests, measured on the render)'
      - name: --ts-chrome-glass-hero
        value: {r: 0.039215688, g: 0.03137255, b: 0.023529412, a: 0.92}
        note: 'The chrome discs and a Glass Navigation Bar over the hero''s picture:
          DARK glass, the same in both modes. No backdrop blur in UI Toolkit, and
          the project blends in LINEAR light: a white mark keeps 7:1 over a white
          sky only on a ground of luminance <= 0.10, measured on the render (PoiCardChromeMarksSceneTests)'
      - name: --ts-chrome-line-hero
        value: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 0.32}
        note: 'The light rim of a chrome disc over the hero (v5): it draws the disc''s
          edge over a dark picture'
      - name: --ts-glass-ground
        value: {r: 0.95686275, g: 0.9411765, b: 0.9098039, a: 0.62}
        note: 'The sheet''s ground between the blocks (R11 tinted glass: light clear,
          dark smoked): tints card_glass.png, a vertical alpha ramp, so the top is
          clearer; this alpha is the ramp''s foot'
      - name: --ts-ink
        value: {r: 0.078431375, g: 0.06666667, b: 0.050980393, a: 1}
        note: 'Text: solid ink only (D1: no alpha on text), every role >= 7:1 on
          every surface it sits on'
      - name: --ts-ink-2
        value: {r: 0.23921569, g: 0.21176471, b: 0.1764706, a: 1}
        note: 
      - name: --ts-ink-3
        value: {r: 0.30980393, g: 0.2784314, b: 0.23529412, a: 1}
        note: 
      - name: --ts-on-accent
        value: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
        note: 
      - name: --ts-accent
        value: {r: 0.11764706, g: 0.22745098, b: 0.5411765, a: 1}
        note: 'Accent: the heritage option of the accent knob (light cobalt, dark
          gold)'
      - name: --ts-accent-text
        value: {r: 0.11764706, g: 0.22745098, b: 0.5411765, a: 1}
        note: 
      - name: --ts-accent-shine
        value: {r: 0.13333334, g: 0.27450982, b: 0.6666667, a: 1}
        note: 'The Open Row shine (R14.8): the brightest colour a light sweeping
          across the words gives them; >= 7:1 on every surface like any text (D1)'
      - name: --ts-accent-2
        value: {r: 0.7882353, g: 0.63529414, b: 0.15294118, a: 1}
        note: 
      - name: --ts-line
        value: {r: 0.43529412, g: 0.4, b: 0.3529412, a: 1}
        note: 'Lines: a border that means something (>= 4.5:1 on the surfaces)'
      - name: --ts-hair
        value: {r: 0.8509804, g: 0.8235294, b: 0.7764706, a: 1}
        note: 'A decorative hairline inside a block (separators): never the only
          cue'
      - name: --ts-metal-edge
        value: {r: 0.2627451, g: 0.23529412, b: 0.19607843, a: 1}
        note: 'The block frame (R13.1, R12.5): the rim''s outer line, measured against
          the sheet ground over the sunny-wall photo (ThemeFrameSceneTests). Dark
          metal in light, light metal in dark: the line or the surface beside it
          clears 3:1 against ANY ground -- light: the white surface up to ground
          luminance 0.30, this line (L 0.048) from 0.24; dark: the surface from 0.13,
          this line (L 0.52) below it'
      - name: --ts-metal-hi
        value: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
        note: The rim's inner band where the light falls (top, left)
      - name: --ts-metal-lo
        value: {r: 0.5411765, g: 0.50980395, b: 0.4627451, a: 1}
        note: 'The rim''s band in shade (bottom, right): with the hi side a clear
          bevel the moving light reads on (_3.3 S4a)'
      - name: --ts-metal-groove
        value: {r: 0.6901961, g: 0.65882355, b: 0.60784316, a: 1}
        note: 'The thin groove just inside the rim''s band (_3.3 S4a): a second metal
          line against the surface, the brushed bands'
      - name: --ts-elevation-1
        value: {r: 0.078431375, g: 0.06666667, b: 0.050980393, a: 0.2}
        note: 'A block''s shadow (tints card_block_shadow.png). Light only: a shadow
          is invisible on a dark ground (R8 S7), dark gets its depth from the surface
          tone'
      - name: --ts-elevation-2
        value: {r: 0.078431375, g: 0.06666667, b: 0.050980393, a: 0.32}
        note: A featured block's shadow
      - name: --ts-status-0
        value: {r: 0.18039216, g: 0.49019608, b: 0.19607843, a: 1}
